
Simple explanation
SHUTDOWN IMMEDIATE → safely stops database activity and closes the database.
STARTUP MOUNT → starts the Oracle instance and mounts the database, but does not open it to users.
In this state, Oracle allows the ARCHIVELOG configuration change.
Then ALTER DATABASE OPEN → brings the database back for normal application/user access.
So, shutdown was required to move the database from OPEN → MOUNT state safely and enable ARCHIVELOG mode.



SELECT log_mode FROM v$database;



